Chapter: Bench JoinExit
  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Definitions

 Every other bench in this directory returns from its arms. That is a shape,
 not a coincidence, and it left the non-tail join exit unmeasured: CL 8600
 taught the fall-through to skip blocks that emit nothing and, by naming the
 exit block one way and the layout another, made each arm emit a five-byte
 jump to the instruction underneath it. All nine benches were green. This one
 was 6 instructions before that change, 7 after, and 6 again once both sides
 canonicalised the same way.

  joinexit : Integer -> Integer
  joinexit (x) = let v = if x > 0 then x + 1 else x - 1 in v

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (joinexit 10))
    print-line-uni (show (joinexit (-10)))
  end

